# CareClinic mobile — Maestro flows — Android

_Generated by StepForge — by Md Zarin Tasnim on 2026-10-15 from the **Emulator** environment._

2 scenarios: Sign in and add a patient, Gestures and device steps.

## Setup

```bash
curl -fsSL "https://get.maestro.mobile.dev" | bash    # Maestro (open source, Apache-2.0; needs Java 17+)
export MAESTRO_CLI_NO_ANALYTICS=1                    # keep Maestro from sending usage data
adb install -r path/to/app.apk                        # the app under test
set -a && . ./.env && set +a                          # secrets (MAESTRO_*) and APP_ID, from .env
cp .env.example .env   # then fill in the values
```

## Run

```bash
maestro test -e APP_ID=$APP_ID flows                     # all flows
maestro test --include-tags smoke flows            # one tag
maestro test --format junit --output results/junit.xml flows
```

## Configuration

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `BASE_URL` | Emulator environment (default `https://api.careclinic.test`) |
| `APK` | {{env.apk}} (default `build/careclinic.apk`) |
| `WARD` | {{env.ward}} (default `North`) |
| `NURSE_PASSWORD` | secret {{secret.nursePassword}} — never commit its value |

Secret values are not part of the export: set them in `.env` locally and as CI secrets in pipelines.

## Layout

- `flows/` — one flow per scenario (one per test case, each with its data as env)
- `flows/steps/` — the steps shared by the test cases of a scenario

## Notes

- Maestro finds an element by its id or its text (label, placeholder); StepForge exports the first locator it can express. XPath and fallback locators are not exported.
- Values: test data, {{env.x}} and {{vars.x}} become Maestro variables; secrets are read from MAESTRO_* environment variables.
- Exported on 2026-10-15; re-export from StepForge after changing the scenarios.

## Needs attention

These steps could not be translated exactly; the code has a `TODO(StepForge)` comment where each one was:

- **Gestures and device steps** — ui.navigate: phone and desktop apps have no pages to open; use a deep link (myapp://…) instead
- **Gestures and device steps** — ui.click: its locators (CSS) do not exist in phone and desktop apps; add an id, text, label or XPath locator
- **Gestures and device steps** — ui.click: image locators (pictures) are not exported; add an id, text, label locator
- **Gestures and device steps** — ui.hover: this is a web-page step; phone and desktop apps have no equivalent
- **Gestures and device steps** — ui.switchTab: this is a web-page step; phone and desktop apps have no equivalent
- **Gestures and device steps** — ui.assert: phone and desktop apps have no URL or page title to check
- : Maestro needs the app's package: set APP_ID when running the flows (the environment names only the app file)
- **Sign in and add a patient**: api steps are not part of Maestro flows (they test the app's screens); export them to an Appium or API target
- **Gestures and device steps**: drag and drop is not exported to Maestro; use swipe with start and end points
- **Gestures and device steps**: Maestro cannot put the app in the background for a while; use stopApp and launchApp
- **Gestures and device steps**: Maestro sets permissions when it launches the app: add `permissions:` to launchApp
- **Gestures and device steps**: Maestro cannot send notifications
- **Gestures and device steps**: menu bars are for desktop apps; Maestro tests phone apps
- **Gestures and device steps**: no locator Maestro can use (an id, text, label or placeholder) for xpath=//*[@text="Save"]
- **Gestures and device steps**: Maestro has no fixed wait (500 ms); wait for an element instead (extendedWaitUntil)
- : GitLab CI is not generated for phone and desktop apps (its shared runners have no emulator, simulator or desktop session); the GitHub Actions workflow is
